  'Tile and grout cleaning is the deep cleaning of hard floors and wet area walls, and in practice it is almost entirely about the grout. Tile is glazed and easy. Grout is cement based and porous, so it absorbs soap, oil, dirt and moisture and holds onto them, which is why a mopped floor can still look grubby along every line. TLB Cleaning cleans tile and grout across the Northern Rivers and the Tweed.',
  'Mopping is the reason it gets worse rather than better. A mop lifts the dirt off the tile and pushes most of it into the grout line, which sits slightly lower and is absorbent. Doing that weekly for years is why the grout in a well-kept bathroom can be darker than the grout in a neglected one.',
];

