  {
    question: 'Why does grout go dark even when the floor is mopped?',
    answer:
      'Partly because of the mopping. Grout sits slightly below the tile surface and is porous, so a mop lifts soil off the glazed tile and deposits a share of it into the grout line along with the dirty water. Over years that builds up inside the material rather than on it, which is why the lines keep darkening in a bathroom that is cleaned every week.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does bleach clean grout?',
